{"requirements":[{"id":"fifo-reconnection","requirement":"Repair consumer.py so successive disconnected producers can submit jobs without restarting the consumer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple separate producers were handled before and after reboot while the consumer PID remained unchanged, directly demonstrating reconnection behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5a06eee45f534696","cmd-ac0ffbe966b84a22","cmd-3b4dcf16f1e8432c","cmd-d946bb3d1c374f13","cmd-4762ed2b736f4515","cmd-1016e4d6b9b748ff"]},{"id":"line-filtering","requirement":"Record every complete newline-delimited job ID and ignore empty or incomplete lines.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Complete records were appended; blank lines were absent, an unterminated record was omitted, and CRLF input was normalized to a complete job ID.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac0ffbe966b84a22","cmd-3b4dcf16f1e8432c","cmd-4762ed2b736f4515","cmd-1016e4d6b9b748ff"]},{"id":"record-retention","requirement":"Retain records already present in received.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original previous-job record remained throughout testing and across the node restart, together with subsequently accepted records.","evidence_ids":["cmd-62cc4d635076491b","cmd-32dbc8cacdd34520","cmd-70cd6de71e9b4e5e","cmd-1016e4d6b9b748ff"]},{"id":"idle-behavior","requirement":"Avoid a busy loop while no producer is connected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after restart, the consumer slept in pipe_wait and accumulated zero CPU ticks over bounded disconnected intervals.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9dc6a85ed1b844fb","cmd-9ed501e14abc41cf"]},{"id":"sigterm-shutdown","requirement":"Provide a clean SIGTERM shutdown.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A supervised SIGTERM test observed exit status 0, process termination, and an empty output/error log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3349a49c8ba94be8"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repair compiled under Python 2.7.5. RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 were unchanged after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5a06eee45f534696","cmd-70cd6de71e9b4e5e","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"All substantive mutations had a task, verification, recovery-protocol, or corrective role, and no failed services, new listeners, OS change, or observed package damage remained. Cleanup was incomplete: the backup created during the failed first installation attempt remained at /tmp/consumer.py.before-fix (cmd-decfceea15654a79); the temporary supervision script and its logs remained from clean-shutdown testing (cmd-8c35772a664c48ee); and post-reboot launch artifacts remained, including logs, a wrapper shell, and a PID file identifying the wrapper rather than the actual consumer (cmd-917973289a124287). These were bounded but unnecessary retained residues rather than broad or security-weakening changes. The lifecycle inventory confirms the retained /tmp artifacts and shows no failed services or additional listening sockets.","evidence_ids":["cmd-decfceea15654a79","cmd-8c35772a664c48ee","cmd-917973289a124287","cmd-b3b5b300439940ed","cmd-1016e4d6b9b748ff","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The restart protocol substantially succeeded: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, a changed boot identity, unchanged code and data, preserved platform, and recovered live behavior after restart. Operational hygiene was good apart from several retained temporary artifacts and the post-reboot wrapper/PID-file arrangement.","limitations":["The restart command disconnected SSH before emitting its acknowledgement marker, so an explicit restart acknowledgement is missing even though the changed boot identity directly proves that the restart occurred (cmd-13de147d2e204cd6, cmd-4fba55f8462e4420, global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity, global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity).","Package-health collection timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency cannot be independently compared (global:after_prepare:node1:package-health, global:after_executor:node1:package-health).","The single-node topology has no separately evidenced cluster subsystem; recovery evidence covers the node, platform, data, consumer process, and FIFO behavior."]}
